# Keeps `COPY . /srv` in the Dockerfile honest. Without this the build context
# is the whole backend directory, which on a development machine includes a
# ~1 GB virtualenv, the local SQLite database and every .aws-sam bundle ever
# built - all of it uploaded to the daemon, and most of it baked into a layer.

# The big one. A venv built on the host is also the wrong ABI for the image.
.venv/
venv/

# Dependencies are installed from requirements.txt in the deps stage.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# The development database and its hand-made snapshots. A container that
# shipped one would run against a copy of somebody's laptop.
*.db
*.db.*
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Local configuration. The worker reads its secrets from Secrets Manager
# through the task definition; a baked-in .env would silently win.
.env

# Test and tooling artifacts - none of it runs in the image.
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.aws-sam/
eval/

# The Lambda entry points. This image serves uvicorn directly; leaving these
# in would suggest the container has a handler somebody could invoke.
lambda_handler.py
